      "text": "A wage deduction for a cash shortage is allowed only if the employer is in a trade, occupation or business where making deductions or requiring deposits to reimburse loss or damage to tools, materials or equipment supplied by the employer is a recognized practice. Then the employee must be clearly shown to be responsible, be given a reasonable chance to explain, the deduction must be fair and not exceed the actual loss, and it cannot be more than 20 % of the employee’s weekly wages.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q1"
        }
      ]
