      "text": "The law defines 13th‑month pay as one‑twelfth (1/12) of an employee’s basic salary for a calendar year; it does not provide a formula for a proportionate amount when the employee leaves before year‑end. The rule applies to all rank‑and‑file workers and requires payment by December 24 each year, but it does not adjust the amount based on the period actually worked.",
