      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "The statutory definition states that 13th‑month pay equals one‑twelfth of the basic salary earned within a calendar year; it gives no guidance on calculating a reduced, proportionate payment for an employee who departs mid‑year. Thus, the available evidence explains only the general rule, not a prorated amount.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q5" },
