    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "The Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) may start an investigation when a consumer submits a petition or a letter‑complaint. The consumer arbitration officer then conducts a hearing, gives notice to the parties, allows them to submit statements or settlement offers, and, if settlement fails, proceeds to formally investigate and decide the case, with a decision required within fifteen (15) days after the investigation ends.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s2.q1" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q2" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q10" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Sa Art. 100, refund lang ang pwede kapag may imperpeksiyon ang produkto na hindi naayos ng supplier sa loob ng 30 araw; pagkatapos, puwedeng piliin ng consumer ang “immediate reimbursement of the amount paid, with monetary updating.” Dahil napili mo lang ang maling kulay at walang sira o depekto, hindi natugunan ang trigger na imperpeksiyon, kaya walang awtomatikong refund sa ilalim ng batas.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q2"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Ayon sa Art. 100, ang consumer ay may karapatang humingi ng refund (kasama ang monetary updating) kung ang produkto ay may imperpeksiyon na hindi naayos ng supplier sa loob ng tatlumpung (30) araw. Kung wala namang depekto—tulad ng pagbabago lang ng gusto mo—hindi nasusunod ang kondisyon ng imperpeksiyon, kaya hindi awtomatikong ibibigay ang refund sa retail transaction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q2"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q4"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "If a seller does not correct the appliance’s imperfection within thirty (30) days after the consumer reports it, the consumer may choose one of three remedies: replacement with a product of the same kind in perfect condition; immediate reimbursement of the amount paid with monetary updating; or a proportionate price reduction. The time limit can be adjusted by agreement, but it may not be reduced below seven (7) days nor extended beyond one hundred and eighty (180) days.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q2" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q3" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q4" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "A consumer can file a petition or letter‑complaint with the Department of Trade and Industry. The department may then open an investigation and, if it finds a prima facie violation, may initiate formal administrative action. The consumer arbitration officer conducts hearings, gives notice of date, time and place, allows parties to submit statements or settlement offers, and if settlement fails, proceeds to investigate and decide the case, with a decision required within fifteen (15) days after the investigation ends.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s2.q1" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q2" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q10" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Omnibus Rules, wages must be paid in legal tender; using vouchers, coupons or any token that pretends to be money is absolutely prohibited, even if the employee asks for it. So a private café cannot legally satisfy wage obligations by giving store‑only vouchers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "The Consumer Act says it is unlawful to sell a consumer product at a price higher than the price publicly displayed on a tag, label or price list. Therefore, a hardware shop that charges more for a toolbox at checkout than the price shown on its shelf or price list is violating the price‑ceiling rule.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Ayon sa No Shortchanging Act of 2016, bawat business establishment ay may tungkulin na ibigay ang eksaktong sukli sa consumer nang hindi hinihintay na hilingin ito. Ipinagbabawal din na mag‑shortchange kahit maliit lang ang halaga, at bawal din mag‑bigay ng sukli sa ibang anyo kaysa sa tunay na pera (hal., papel o barya). Kung hindi sinusunod ito, illegal ang gawain.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s2.q1"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s2.q2"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s2.q4"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "For a covered employee, every employer must provide a rest period of at least twenty‑four (24) consecutive hours after each stretch of six consecutive normal work days. This is the minimum weekly rest requirement; it does not depend on how many days the employee actually worked, only that the rest follows six straight work days.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Where a service supplier delivers services that are imperfect—meaning they are not fit for the purpose reasonably expected or do not match the advertised description—the supplier is liable. The consumer may choose any of the following remedies: the supplier must perform the service again at no extra cost, reimburse the amount paid with monetary updating, or grant a proportionate price reduction; the re‑performance may be done by a qualified third party at the supplier’s risk and cost.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q1"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q2"
        },
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q3"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Ayon sa No Shortchanging Act of 2016, obligadong ibigay ng anumang business establishment ang eksaktong sukli sa consumer nang hindi hinihintay na hilingin ito. Ipinagbabawal din na mag‑shortchange kahit maliit lang ang halaga, at bawal mag‑bigay ng sukli sa ibang anyo kaysa sa tunay na pera (hal., papel o barya).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote_id": "concern_001.s2.q1"
        },
